<title>BELGIUM: Austria seeks EU aid for cereal transport to ports.</title>
<headline>Austria seeks EU aid for cereal transport to ports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Austrian application for payment to cover the cost of shipping cereals to European Union borders will be considered by cereals experts on Thursday, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Austria is landlocked and is only paid under existing legislation for transporting cereals to its own borders. The Austrians feel they are disadvantaged and the Commission has expressed support for their application,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The item is not listed for a vote at Thursday's cereals management committee which follows the experts group meeting.</p>
</text>
